00:00:03.409 --> 00:00:05.630 align:start position:0%
six weeks to the day of Olivia Pratt  corbell's death the man accused of her  murder was brought to court in Liverpool  34 year old Thomas Cashman lives just  two miles from Olivia's home where late  that August night he's alleged to have  shot and killed her the nine-year-old  died from a gunshot wound to the chest  her death sending a wave of shock  through the community and across the  country and sparking a huge  investigation  police said a convicted burglar called  Joseph knee had forced his way into the  family home after seeing Olivia's mother  Cheryl had opened the front door a  gunman fired several shots into the  house killing Olivia Thomas Cashman is  also accused of the attempted murder of  Cheryl and knee and the possession of  firearms with the intent to endanger  life  also in court were members of Olivia's  family including her Father John and her  mother Cheryl throughout proceedings  they stared across the courtroom at  Thomas Cashman in the dock he sat head  bowed at times handcuffed and surrounded  by police officers he said nothing  Beyond confirming his identity  a second man also appeared in court  charged with assisting an offender  40-year-old Paul Russell is alleged to  have driven the gunman away from the  scene that night and disposed of his  clothing  the community Olivia called home  continues to mourn her death merseyside  police have thanked the public for what  they call their overwhelming support of  the investigation an investigation they  say that continues  Thomas Cashman was driven from Court  having been remanded in custody he was  told he will stand trial for Olivia's  murder in March Greg Milam Sky News  Liverpool
 

